<title>SINGAPORE: SIA orders Airbus equipment.</title>
<headline>SIA orders Airbus equipment.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines (SIA) has become the first customer for Airbus Industrie's future navigation system datalink, AIM FANS A (FANS), Airbus said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The statement said SIA had made &quot;a multi-million dollar order to equip all of its A340 fleet&quot; with FANS. Airbus and SIA spokesmen said they could not give further details on the order's value. SIA has eight Airbus A340s in its fleet.</p>
<p>FANS comprises satellite navigation, a datalink between aircraft and ground, and better air traffic management for controllers, Airbus said. -- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
